{"page": 2, "text": "Primary drivers of the changes in the table above were as follows: Revenue: The quarter change was primarily driven by normal fluctuations, partially offset by an increase in average reimbursement rates and improvements in payor mix. The year to date change was driven by typical annual rate increases and other normal fluctuations, partially offset by unfavorable changes in payor mix. Patient care costs: The quarter change was primarily due to increased medical supplies expenses. The year to date change was primarily driven by increased compensation expenses, medical supplies expense, insurance costs and health benefits expenses. General and administrative: The quarter change was primarily due to decreased professional fees. The year to date change was primarily driven by increases in IT-related costs and compensation expenses, partially offset by costs related to the cybersecurity incident experienced by the Company in 2025. Certain items impacting the quarter: Goodwill and other asset impairment charges. During the quarter ended September 30, 2026, we recognized non-cash goodwill and other asset impairment charges related to our business in China. The effect was a $62 million impairment charge within operating income, offset by a $1 million tax benefit and $34 million noncontrolling interest credit, resulting in a $27 million net income impact attributable to DaVita Inc. Share repurchases. During the three months ended September 30, 2026, we repurchased 0.6 million shares for $111 million, at an average price paid of $186.21 per share. Subsequent to September 30, 2026 through October 27, 2026, the Company has repurchased 0.5 million shares of our common stock for $87 million at an average price paid of $180.57 per share. Financial and operating metrics:\nThree months ended\nSeptember 30, Twelve months ended\nSeptember 30,\n2026 2025 2026 2025\nCash flow: (dollars in millions)\nOperating cash flow $ 519 $ 842 $ 1,870 $ 1,893\nFree cash flow(1) $